# No `rg` in the shell

This machine does **not** have `rg` / ripgrep on PATH. Do not run `rg` (or `ripgrep`) via the Shell tool or in copy-paste commands for the user.

## What to use instead

1. **Agent search** — Cursor `Grep` / `Glob` tools (these are fine; they are not the shell `rg` binary).
2. **User-facing PowerShell** — `Select-String` / `Get-ChildItem -Recurse` when a pasteable search command is needed.
3. **User-facing bash (Linux host)** — `grep -R` / `find` when that is where they are working.

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD — shell or paste block
rg -n "where_used" src
rg --files -g "*.py"

# ✅ GOOD — agent uses Grep/Glob tools
# ✅ GOOD — PowerShell for the user
Select-String -Path src\creopdm\**\*.py -Pattern "where_used"
Get-ChildItem -Path src -Recurse -Filter *.py
```
